It builds on work by KingKong Tech, released under Apache-2.0:
  - https://github.com/KingKongRobotics/jumper        (training toolkit and robot model)
  - https://github.com/KingKongRobotics/jumper-design (scene and skin tools, original Jumper skin)

What is derived from that work, and where:
  - 3_SKIN/jumper_neon.xml is a modified copy of jumper/assets/jumper/jumper.xml: only colours
    and materials were changed (see 3_SKIN/make_neon_skin.py).
  - 2_SCENE/crab_rave.map is a scene package exported with the jumper-design tools. It embeds
    KingKong's original Jumper skin and robot meshes together with the license and attribution
    notices that ship inside that archive; those notices stay with the archive.
  - 4_TRAINING/ holds a policy checkpoint and ONNX export trained with the jumper toolkit on its
    demonstration dance. The dance choreography itself is KingKong's demo choreography; it is not
    ours and is not included here.

Not included: the two repositories above, the Python environments, any music.
The videos in 1_FINAL_VIDEOS/ are silent.

